# Recut Software License

**Free for individuals and small teams · Larger organizations require a company license**

Copyright © 2026 Recut ("we" / "Licensor")

Depending on the type of your legal entity, you are granted permission to use Recut for your project. Individuals and small companies are allowed to use Recut to create videos for free (even commercially), while a company license is required for for-profit organizations of a certain size. This two-tier system was designed to ensure funding for this project while still keeping the source code available and the program free for most.

- [Free License](#free-license)
- [Company License](#company-license)

## Scope and acceptance

This license (the "License") covers the Recut software, including the Recut platform (service, App Host, media platform, website and install scripts) and all official Apps and their documentation (including but not limited to AI Short Film, Audio Studio, Cover Studio, Depth Maps, the timeline Editor and Remotion Studio) (together, the "Software").

By using, copying, modifying or distributing the Software, you accept this License. If you do not accept the terms of this License, you may not use the Software.

## Free License

### Eligibility

You are eligible to use Recut for free if you are:

- an individual;
- a for-profit organization with up to 3 employees;
- a non-profit or not-for-profit organization;
- evaluating whether Recut is a good fit, and not yet using it in a commercial way.

### Allowed use cases

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person eligible for the "Free License", to use the Software non-commercially or commercially for the purpose of creating videos and images, and to modify the Software to their own liking, for the purpose of fulfilling their custom use case or to contribute bug fixes or improvements back to Recut.

### Disallowed use cases

It is not allowed to copy or modify Recut code for the purpose of selling, renting, licensing, relicensing, or sublicensing your own derivative of Recut.

### Warranty notice

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

### Support

Support is provided on a best-we-can-do basis via GitHub Issues and the official community.

## Company License

You are required to obtain a Company License to use Recut if you are not within the group of entities eligible for the Free License. This license enables you to use Recut for the allowed use cases specified in the Free License, and gives you access to prioritized support.

Pricing and purchase: https://recut.video | license@recut.video

